9	16	22	23	Ragged Dick	9	" Wake up there , youngster , "
47	55	57	58	the man	17	" Wake up , you young vagabond ! "
63	80	57	58	the man	17	" I suppose you 'd lay there all day , if I had n't called you . "
81	87	89	89	Dick	9	" What time is it ? "
91	95	57	58	the man	17	" Seven o'clock . "
96	137	57	58	the man	17	" Seven o'clock ! I oughter've been up an hour ago . I know what ' twas made me so precious sleepy . I went to the Old Bowery last night , and did n't turn in till past twelve . "
138	153	155	156	the man	17	" You went to the Old Bowery ? Where 'd you get your money ? "
174	201	160	172	a porter in the employ of a firm doing business on Spruce Street	19	" Made it by shines , in course . My guardian do n't allow me no money for theatres , so I have to earn it . "
202	211	213	214	the porter	21	" Some boys get it easier than that , "
217	233	235	235	Dick	9	" You do n't catch me stealin ' , if that 's what you mean , "
237	246	57	58	the man	17	" Do n't you ever steal , then ? "
247	266	160	172	a porter in the employ of a firm doing business on Spruce Street	19	" No , and I would n't . Lots of boys does it , but I would n't . "
267	293	57	58	the man	17	" Well , I 'm glad to hear you say that . I believe there 's some good in you , Dick , after all . "
294	303	305	305	Dick	9	" Oh , I 'm a rough customer ! "
307	318	305	305	Dick	9	" But I would n't steal . It 's mean . "
319	329	57	58	the man	17	" I 'm glad you think so , Dick , "
340	351	57	58	the man	17	" Have you got any money to buy your breakfast ? "
352	362	57	58	the man	17	" No , but I 'll soon get some . "
743	750	728	728	he	9	" Shine yer boots , sir ? "
751	755	757	758	a gentleman	27	" How much ? "
766	770	772	772	Dick	9	" Ten cents , "
800	811	757	758	a gentleman	27	" Ten cents ! Is n't that a little steep ? "
812	823	825	825	Dick	9	" Well , you know ' taint all clear profit , "
834	855	825	825	Dick	9	" There 's the _ blacking _ costs something , and I have to get a new brush pretty often . "
856	865	867	868	the gentleman	30	" And you have a large rent too , "
883	888	890	890	Dick	9	" Yes , sir , "
897	938	890	890	Dick	9	" I have to pay such a big rent for my manshun up on Fifth Avenoo , that I ca n't afford to take less than ten cents a shine . I 'll give you a bully shine , sir . "
939	963	867	868	the gentleman	30	" Be quick about it , for I am in a hurry . So your house is on Fifth Avenue , is it ? "
964	971	973	973	Dick	9	" It is n't anywhere else , "
982	989	991	992	the gentleman	30	" What tailor do you patronize ? "
999	1010	1012	1012	Dick	9	" Would you like to go to the same one ? "
1016	1035	867	868	the gentleman	30	" Well , no ; it strikes me that he did n't give you a very good fit . "
1036	1045	1047	1047	Dick	9	" This coat once belonged to General Washington , "
1051	1126	1047	1047	Dick	9	" He wore it all through the Revolution , and it got torn some , 'cause he fit so hard . When he died he told his widder to give it to some smart young feller that had n't got none of his own ; so she gave it to me . But if you 'd like it , sir , to remember General Washington by , I 'll let you have it reasonable . "
1127	1152	867	868	the gentleman	30	" Thank you , but I would n't want to deprive you of it . And did your pants come from General Washington too ? "
1153	1187	1047	1047	Dick	9	" No , they was a gift from Lewis Napoleon . Lewis had outgrown 'em and sent 'em to me,--he 's bigger than me , and that 's why they do n't fit . "
1188	1209	867	868	the gentleman	30	" It seems you have distinguished friends . Now , my lad , I suppose you would like your money . "
1210	1218	1220	1220	Dick	9	" I should n't have any objection , "
1222	1226	1228	1229	the gentleman	30	" I believe , "
1237	1256	1228	1229	the gentleman	30	" I have n't got anything short of twenty - five cents . Have you got any change ? "
1257	1262	1264	1264	Dick	9	" Not a cent , "
1266	1277	1264	1264	Dick	9	" All my money 's invested in the Erie Railroad . "
1278	1283	867	868	the gentleman	30	" That 's unfortunate . "
1284	1294	1264	1264	Dick	9	" Shall I get the money changed , sir ? "
1295	1334	867	868	the gentleman	30	" I ca n't wait ; I 've got to meet an appointment immediately . I 'll hand you twenty - five cents , and you can leave the change at my office any time during the day . "
1335	1345	1264	1264	Dick	9	" All right , sir . Where is it ? "
1346	1357	867	868	the gentleman	30	" No . 125 Fulton Street . Shall you remember ? "
1358	1366	1264	1264	Dick	9	" Yes , sir . What name ? "
1367	1373	867	868	the gentleman	30	" Greyson,--office on second floor . "
1374	1385	1264	1264	Dick	9	" All right , sir ; I 'll bring it . "
1386	1397	1399	1400	Mr. Greyson	13	" I wonder whether the little scamp will prove honest , "
1409	1441	1399	1400	Mr. Greyson	13	" If he does , I 'll give him my custom regularly . If he do n't as is most likely , I sha n't mind the loss of fifteen cents . "
1545	1561	1563	1564	Ragged Dick	9	" I guess he would n't want to stay long if he did get in , "
1571	1605	1563	1564	Ragged Dick	9	" Leastways I should n't . They 're so precious glad to see you that they wo n't let you go , but board you gratooitous , and never send in no bills . "
